    {
      "name": "glossary",
      "displayName": "Business Glossary",
      "pageType": "PAGE_TYPE_CANVAS",
      "layoutVersion": "GRID_V1",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {"name": "gloss-header", "multilineTextboxSpec": {"lines": ["# Business Glossary\n", "\n", "Plain-language definitions for every figure on this dashboard. All figures are from a synthetic sample."]}},
          "position": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 12, "height": 2}
        },
        {
          "widget": {"name": "gloss-margin", "multilineTextboxSpec": {"lines": [
            "### Net margin and margin rate (THE fixed definition)\n",
            "\n",
            "**Net margin** = sales after discounts, less returns, less cost of goods sold. Discounts are never subtracted a second time.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Margin rate** = net margin ÷ sales after returns. On this data: **30.83%**.\n",
            "\n",
            "A second figure sometimes appears — net margin ÷ a different sales total (28.95% on this data). That is the **same dollars, different denominator**. It is shown for reference only and is never the headline rate. This is exactly the kind of inconsistency that made the board unable to trust a single loyalty or margin number — one definition, used everywhere, fixes it."
          ]}},
          "position": {"x": 0, "y": 2, "width": 6, "height": 7}
        },
        {
          "widget": {"name": "gloss-estimates", "multilineTextboxSpec": {"lines": [
            "### What “ESTIMATE” means here\n",
            "\n",
            "**Promotion margin below baseline**: the modeled gap between a promotion's actual margin per day and a baseline sell-through rate. It is a comparison to a model, not a cash measurement — call it “below baseline,” never “lost” or “saved.”\n",
            "\n",
            "**Stock-out margin**: sales are not generated to dip during a stock-out in this synthetic sample, so this is a modeled estimate of what empty shelves may be costing, not a measured effect.\n",
            "\n",
            "Both are labelled ESTIMATE everywhere they appear, and both combine into the single **“margin at risk before the next peak”** figure on the Key Figures page."
          ]}},
          "position": {"x": 6, "y": 2, "width": 6, "height": 7}
        },
        {
          "widget": {"name": "gloss-sources", "multilineTextboxSpec": {"lines": [
            "### Data sources (assumed, synthetic)\n",
            "\n",
            "- **Point-of-sale transaction files** (daily export) — explains why a file arriving twice can double-count revenue, and why reprocessing needs to be safe.\n",
            "- **Weekly inventory snapshot feed**, per store and product — the basis for stock-out exposure.\n",
            "- **Loyalty file**, from the program vendor — the basis for retention.\n",
            "- **Promotions calendar** — the basis for promotion effectiveness.\n",
            "\n",
            "All data in this build is synthetic, generated with a fixed seed. No real customer, employer or confidential data is used anywhere."
          ]}},
          "position": {"x": 0, "y": 9, "width": 6, "height": 6}
        },
        {
          "widget": {"name": "gloss-scope", "multilineTextboxSpec": {"lines": [
            "### What this build does and does not do\n",
            "\n",
            "**Built**: the pipeline counts, quarantines and reports bad rows, duplicates and late arrivals (see the trust tile and this page's data trust recap).\n",
            "\n",
            "**Not built — pilot additions**: automated alerting on bad data, schema-change detection, access-control enforcement, and promotion attribution modeling. Unity Catalog grants (see sql/grants.sql) show the mechanism for access control; enforcement workflows are a pilot addition, not demonstrated here.\n",
            "\n",
            "Customer email and phone fields in the source data are synthetic placeholders for a governance conversation, not real data."
          ]}},
          "position": {"x": 6, "y": 9, "width": 6, "height": 6}
        }
      ]
    },
